{"id": "EUVD-2026-106917", "enisaUuid": "509e13e9-1d25-39b3-b320-5695bbc1219a", "description": "Vyper 0.1.0b1 before 0.1.0b12, 0.1.0b14, and 0.4.1 through 0.5.0b1 mix character-based line offsets with Python's UTF-8 byte col_offset values in vyper/ast/parse.py, so multi-byte characters shift the source slices used to reconstruct later numeric literals. An attacker contributing source with non-ASCII identifiers that NFKC-normalize to ASCII, or an invisible byte-order mark, can silently substitute addresses, integers or other constants in compiled code.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T00:37:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T00:37:12", "baseScore": 6.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/vyperlang/vyper/security/advisories/GHSA-r3c7-7xwm-6vfw", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vyper-through-0.5-0b1-literal-value-substitution-via-multi-byte-characters"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-114114", "GHSA-vchg-h45q-h36m"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4931d3f0-b50c-3b6a-94b6-5bff45872d08", "product": {"name": "vyper", "vendor": {"name": "vyperlang"}}, "product_version": "0.1.0b1 <0.1.0b12"}, {"id": "6bd56374-b1fc-3a76-9bdd-35ef9f4596d0", "product": {"name": "vyper", "vendor": {"name": "vyperlang"}}, "product_version": "0.4.1 \u22640.5.0b1"}, {"id": "eb121d64-13f3-36dc-93d2-2f8841ea834e", "product": {"name": "vyper", "vendor": {"name": "vyperlang"}}, "product_version": "0.1.0b14 <0.1.0b15"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5e523123-f7ef-35a1-afa5-0fba245c1041", "vendor": {"name": "vyperlang"}}], "isExploited": false}